<title>INDIA: Indian soybean ends up on strong demand.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean ends up on strong demand.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1997-04-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices ended Friday up on good demand from processing plants, traders said.</p>
<p>They said prices rose 200-300 rupees per tonne in moderate trade. Arrivals were poor and the undertone strong, they said.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices rose 100 rupees per tonne on limited supply in light trade and a firm undertone, traders said.</p>
<p>Soymeal and rapeseed extraction prices were little changed. Soymeal yellow was $320-321 per tonne FAS (Free alongside Ship) in western Indian ports in bulk for export.</p>
<p>Rapeseed extraction was $121-122 per tonne FAS in bulk for export and 4,250 rupees per tonne in FOR (Free on Rail) condition, traders said.</p>
<p>Business volumes were dull and the undertone strong, they said.</p>
